.title = "A Rambling Review of DOOM: The Dark Ages",
.date = @date("2026-02-03T19:00:00+1000"),
.author = "Garrett Moseke",
.layout = "post.shtml",
.draft = false,
.description = "Hello would you like to meet our lord and savior MY CHAINSAW SHIELD IN YOUR FACE",
.tags = ["Rambling Review", "Video Games"]
---

Allow me to describe the story of DOOM: The Dark Ages (henceforth "TDA") as succinctly as possible:

So there's this demon twink guy right and he wants like ultimate evil power or something
right and there's this witch lady from another dimension where Cthulu lives who's
whispering in his ear. So anyway he attacks the Space Spartans and you, the Doomslayer
(not a Space Spartan) go destroy his army with a chainsaw shield and various heavy weaponry. But
then he goes for the magic doohickey that will let him be super powerful but the king of
the Space Spartans gets it first but the demon twink kicks his ass but then you
(Doomslayer) get there and save the king. Then the witch lady summons a giant tentacle
monster from the Cthulu realm and it kidnaps the princess of the Space Spartans so you go
free a skyscraper-sized Cthulu thing and ride on its back into the other dimension
(because this is a good video game) where you save her and now apparently she's like the
most powerful being in existence? But then the elder gods trap you in a cage so you blow
yourself up to escape and now you're a zombie in the afterlife but you're too angry to let
that stop you so you blast your way to the boat of the damned and shoot your way out of the afterlife
(because this is a good video game). Anyway you go back to the Space Spartans and these
other aliens that were kinda in control of you have now allied with demon twink so you
teleport onto their ship and beat the shit out of their fat leader who looks like one of
the people in WALL-E. Then the demon twink invades with the ultimate power he stole from
Spartan Princess so you pilot a giant mech and also a dragon with laser wings through the
battlefield and fight a giant cyborg Cthulu elder god (because this is a good video game)
and then you fight the demon twink but he's kinda gross and pasty now. So you kick his ass
and he runs away like a little bitch so you chase him into Hell and fight your way through
his flagship where you kick his ass again (this time while also introducing the alternate
dimension witch lady to your chainsaw shield) and then the Space Spartans hold a like
vigil for you but you're still alive and you're now making your way through Hell turning
everything that moves into a fine red mist.

Now allow me to do the same for DOOM: 2016:

Some energy scientists joined a cult and now there are a bunch of demons on Mars. You are
provided a shotgun with which to solve this problem. Cue music.

Just to really hammer it home:
* In DOOM 2016 the final boss is the spider mastermind, a slightly larger demon.
* In DOOM: Eternal the final boss is the Icon of Sin, a giant demon titan. The stakes are
slightly higher too, there's demons on earth now! And also we go to space? [And shoot a
hole in Mars!](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-u1H0gltsbw)
* In DOOM: The Dark Ages you fight dozens of giant demon titans in the third level. And
pilot a dragon with laser wings. And teleport between dimensions. And fight Cthulu.

The best description I can come up with for TDA is "unabashedly over the top." It is pedal
all the way through the metal and through the pavement too while it's at it. I can forgive
the eyeroll-inducing story (partly because the Doomslayer himself does not give a flying
fuck about what's going on around him unless it involves a demon being ripped and/or torn)
becasue the moment-to-moment gameplay is *chef's kiss*. They've done the impossible and
made the combat loop from DOOM: Eternal even more fun by giving you the ability to dash
across the entire combat field and vaporize anything in the way. I saw some ~insane
people~ strangers online claiming that the combat loop is slow and boring. I think they
purchased a different video game, because it is the exact opposite. If you are not moving
at all times you are dead. If you are not swapping weapons at all time you are dead. If
you are not beating the everloving shit out of anything that moves with your gauntlet
everytime it is charged, you are dead. Maybe it was because of the higher difficulty I
played the game on, but I found it to be constant mayhem. Excellent, perfect mayhem.

As a last couple notes, it's incredibly well optimized, which is a very welcome rarity
among triple-A games nowadays. My desktop is a micro-itx build in a tiny little case, and
even though the thermals aren't bad by any means my CPU happily sat at only ~80C the
entire time I was playing, on high settings, always 90+ fps. Magic. Please take notes
everyone else.

Finally, the soundtrack you didn't quite feel in your bones as much as Mick Gordon's
tracks, but it still did what it was supposed to do, which is get you good and in the zone
of demon-bashing. Sadly, I've found nowhere to purchase it standalone (the version on
steam apparently comes with a dedicated launcher to DRM control it because we can't have
nice things), so I'll have to leave it be for now.

In the next DOOM game the Doomslayer is going to pilot a planet sized mech and then blow
up the galaxy with a shotgun, mark my words.
